  "notes": "This batch implements the New Ideas 4-14 source map's recommended bounded offline bitemporal verification-state replay. It preserves independent effective and recorded time, append order, correction, re-verification, supersession, revocation, unknown history, deterministic hashing, parser bounds, and a strict rule that every non-active state blocks ANSWER while ACTIVE remains insufficient by itself. It does not resolve evidence refs, create EvidenceBundles, decide policy, record human review, issue corrections, select releases, render a UI, activate a source, promote, release, deploy, or publish. Rollback is a clean revert of the feature commit; no stored data or public state requires migration."
